{"@context":["https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/ns/content/v1.jsonld",{"@base":"https://litlfred.github.io/folio/"}],"@id":"papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/prop-q-heat-equation-exists","@type":["folio-assistant-core:Proposition","doco:Section"],"label":"prop:q-heat-equation-exists","kind":"proposition","title":"Existence and uniqueness for the $q$-heat equation","uses":["papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/def-q-heat-equation"],"proofs":["papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/prf-q-heat-equation-exists"],"tags":["existence","q-heat-equation","well-posedness"],"leanRef":"qou:QOU.QHeatEquation.exists_solution","text":"q-heat-equation-exists.md","leanSource":"q-heat-equation-exists.lean","provenance":"authored","html":"<p><a id=\"prop:q-heat-equation-exists\"></a>\n<strong>Proposition.</strong> <em>Existence and uniqueness for the <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">q</code>-heat equation</em></p>\n<p>Let <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">(\\mathbf{C}, \\varTheta, G, \\mathcal{S})</code> be a quantum observable universe with initial data <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">u_0 \\colon \\mathcal{S} \\to \\mathbf{1}_{\\mathbf{C}}</code>. There exists a formal solution <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">u(t)</code> of the <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">q</code>-heat equation <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\partial_t u = -\\Delta_q u</code> with <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">u(0) = u_0</code>.</p>\n"}
